  "foaf:name": "Pacific Islands Heritage Marine Reserve",
  "sdo:name": "Pacific Islands Heritage Marine Reserve",
  "sdo:description": "The Pacific Islands Heritage Coalition is a diverse network of elders, fishers, cultural practitioners, scientists, navigators, storytellers, nonprofit leaders, community groups, and others across the Pacific. The Coalition formed in 2014 to protect and amplify the cultural and ecological legacy of the Pacific Islands Heritage Marine National Monument (PIHMNM), which spans 1.27 million sq km. PIHMNM contains some of the last wild, healthy ocean ecosystems on the planet and is a place of great cultural significance for Indigenous Pacific Islanders. It is home to endangered and threatened wildlife, including sharks, rays, seabirds, blue whale, leatherback turtle, and deep-sea life found nowhere else. This project focuses on maintaining and expanding protections for this special area and supporting cultural, scientific, and storytelling efforts. The long-term vision is a connected, healthy Pacific where wildlife and communities thrive, and we care for the natural world as our ancestors.",
